Report preserved unchanged. Best source restored according to measured raw and quality.\n\n166/167/168 Taylordegree1/2/3 fail30/27/19 cases, worst nRMSE .0432413/.0341142/.0169094.169/170 classmatmul versions same accuracy but faster (.07135/.11843 localmean). Reject approximation: broad coupling still needs sufficiently precise pair weights, structured lowdegree compression loses geometry.171 degree4 classmatmul prepared to bound quality vs computational cost, not screenedyet. Measured best162 unchanged.\n\n171 Taylordegree4 passes27/30, worst nRMSE .0110019202, mean local time .2812133. Reject: still inaccurate and slower than dense exact coupling. This bounds the structuredpolynomial compression hypothesis; increasingdegree is not promising for performance.\n\n165 fusedaddmm feature geometry andbaddbmm class geometry selected for fourth full official run (session9863). Fresh round4 median .0645664 compared162 .0632217, close enough to test formal fusedgeometry.165 all30 local valid worst .0039617994. Current165 temporary, measured best162 snapshot remains available. No concurrent numerical workloads during official timing. Generated episode4 index summarizes46 source snapshots126-171,39 localall30 valid and7 failing, with exact source hashes and completed official outcomes. Update it after165 finishes.\n\n165 fourth full official result {\"status\": \"ok\", \"raw_metric\": 0.07197932919904512, \"score\": 0.8619749345688746, \"quality_valid\": true, \"method_sha256\": \"45380e25239e9c12ec4828fcf80f9314d981ca792c4d485523e4e7849f6bcae7\", \"result_path\": \"/opt/public_eval/results/d067736a62f94f8e93821ba13720d531.json\"}. Exact report copied unchanged. Final measured best 162_precomputed_norm_geometry restored.\n\nFinal profile on public303_gaussian016: .06931 seconds (local diagnostic, not score). Point dual .022s, class costs .021s, dense coupling .007s.146Torchsum reductions .009s,145mul_ .006s; value overhead .015s includes geometry/indexing. Final exact measur