s officialraw0.0385948 became the first newbest.\n- **537–542, cached empirical point variance and budget reallocation:** restoring an earlier coarse point update with exact variance statistics improves worstnRMSE to0.006117. Hard8/16 variants pass0.008646. Pointlate4 fails22, hard8late4 fails13. Classlate4 variant542 passes0.008906 but statistics and extra work remain slower; reject for speed.\n- **548–558, exact coupling cancellation and kernel dispatch:** all30 pass. Bare GEMV548–552 was very slow and variable. Two-dimensional GEMM553–555 restores speed; shared554 passes officialraw0.0376010 and becomes newbest. Single-batch BMM556/557 and hybrid558 are slower.\n- **559–561, actual column-major coupling storage:** all30 pass, but fresh medians0.0496/0.0531 lose to5540.0426. A stride diagnostic showed transpose-only555 keeps original row-major strides; preserve it as a unary-expression control, not a physical layout change. Explicit `empty((m,n)).T` plus out= creates the real column layout.\n- **562–564, exact low-rank cost energy:** all30 pass with worstnRMSE0.00702565–0.00702570. One22-column GEMM is faster than splitting12+10. Freshround5 medians5540.042632,5620.042365,5640.041586 justified one final complete official564 evaluation.\n\n## Validation, artifacts and continuation\n\nSynthetic checks use18 permutations of public arrays (two public seeds, three settings, three independent permutations), with canonical targets freshly computed by saved initial source000. Sources432/547/512/554/555 all pass18 with worstnRMSE about0.00851313, minimumrho0.99995404 and top0.994667. 564 also passes18, with its original records in episode9_energy_shuffle_stress.json. These are diagnostics, not protected targets or evaluator scores; no tuning was done against them.\n\n'\"'''+f'''- **{len(index)} source snapshots**, **{sum(len(q.get('local_records',[]))==30 for q in index.values())} complete all30 local screens**, **{sum(q.get('local_summary',{{}}).get('valid',False) for q in index.values())} valid sources**, **{sum(q.get('local_summary',{{}}).get('valid') is False for q in index.values())} failed sources**, and **{len(official)} complete official evaluations**.\n'''+'''- Builders1–13, manifests, per-case screenJSON/logs, five alternating fresh-process benchmark rounds, stress scripts/results, starting/final profiles, failed sources and original reports remain in \"'`/tmp/research_history`.\n- episode_9_index.json contains every source/hash and local/official evidence; episode9_official_summary.json and episode_9_final_selection.json preserve exact source selection. Run `python /tmp/research_history/episode9_index.py --restore` to reproduce best-source restoration.\n- A final profile excludes NPZ reads by loading all arguments before timing. Its timing is diagnostic only; no formal score should be inferred from it.\n- Next research should begin from the selected exact source and profile it. Kernel dispatch, matrix layout and cost-energy factorization are productive exact mechanisms. More aggressive finite-schedule truncation, frozen class graphs, Gaussian class geometry, generic grouping and polynomial coupling already have extensive failures or slow controls in prior notes. Read those summaries before revisiting them.\n\nNo protected assets, evaluator code, protected targets, private cases, credentials, environment variables, other trajectories, network, external packages or subagents were accessed. Onlymethod.py changed in the submission. Frozen solve.sh remains byte-identical, and the submission directory contains exactly these two files.\n'\"'''\n(root/'episode_9_continuing_notes.md').write_text(notes);Path('/tmp/research_notes.md').write_text(notes);print('Wrote final continuing notes for',best['name'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
